extends layout
include partials/pagehead

block content
  +pagehead("The house", "We buy the buildings nobody else wants to take on.", "A mill with a listed frontage and a hole in the roof is a hard purchase and a harder conversion. It is also the only way to get a fourteen foot ceiling and a north window wall in a district where land is spoken for.", hero)

  section.band.page
    .detail-grid
      .prose
        h2 What we look for
        p Structure first. A frame that can carry a floor load without being rebuilt, a column grid wide enough to leave open, and glazing on more than one elevation. Those three things decide whether a building converts into something worth living in or an expensive compromise with small rooms.
        p After that, the street. We buy on a small number of streets in a small number of districts and we go back to them, because the second building on a street is always easier than the first. We already know the planning officer, the party wall history and which contractor turns up.
        h2 What we will not do
        p We do not buy for yield and we do not flip. A conversion takes us between two and four years, and we hold most of what we finish. That is why the portfolio is small and why we can afford to tell you what is wrong with a building.
        p We give no investment advice and we make no representation about what a building is worth or what it will return. Where a market requires estate agency registration or anti money laundering checks, we state our position at its actual stage rather than implying one we do not hold.
      aside.aside
        h2 Why buy from an owner
        p There is no chain. We are not waiting on our own purchase, so a completion date means something when we give you one.
        p There is no agent between you and the answer. The floor plates, the load ratings, the service charge history and the survey are in this office.
        a.button(href="/portfolio") See what is available
        a.button.button-quiet(href="/register") Register an interest

  section.band.band-rule.band-raised
    .page
      .section-head
        div
          p.eyebrow How it goes
          h2 Four steps, and we do not skip the first
      ol.steps
        li
          div
            h3 Register once
            p Tell us what you need and where. We read every one and answer within two working days. Approval opens exact addresses, full terms, floor plans and the documents behind them.
        li
          div
            h3 Ask us anything
            p We hold the survey, the title and the service charge history. You get the answer in one message rather than after a call to a client.
        li
          div
            h3 View it with someone who knows it
            p Every viewing is walked by a member of this office. We will tell you where the damp was and what we did about it.
        li
          div
            h3 Agree terms and complete
            p Money moves only after we have approved your application, for an amount we have set, inside a window we have opened. There is no other payment route on this site.

  section.band.band-rule.page
    .stack
      h2 A building usually goes before we advertise it
      p.lede Registering takes a few minutes and puts you on the list that hears first.
      .button-row
        a.button(href="/register") Register an interest
        a.button.button-quiet(href="/contact") Speak to someone
